1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,600
Hello?

2
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,348
Hi. It's Laura Carlton here.

3
00:00:02,348 --> 00:00:05,800
We've just arrived at the holiday flat

4
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:08,640
but I can't get the hot water and heating to work.

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:12,650
Oh right! That's easy. Don't worry.

6
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,780
In the upstairs cupboard, you'll find the water heater.

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:20,110
You'll see three main controls on the left at the bottom of the heater.

8
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:23,620
The first one. The round one on the far left

9
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:27,180
Is the most important one for the heating and hot water.

10
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:31,500
It's the main control switch. Make sure it's in the 'on' position.

11
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,240
The switch itself doesn't light up

12
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:37,630
but the little square below will be black if the switch is 'off'.

13
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:41,820
That's probably what's happened. It's got switched off by mistake.

14
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,540
The middle one of these three controls

15
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:49,000
you'll see it's slightly larger than the first one - controls the radiators.

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
If you feel cold while you're there and need the radiators on

17
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,240
this needs to be turned to maximum.

18
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:58,360
The last of the three controls. The one on the right

19
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,786
Is usually on about a number for setting

20
00:01:00,786 --> 00:01:04,700
which for the water in the taps is usually quite hot enough.

21
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:10,440
Below the heating controls in the middle is a small round plastic button.

22
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,950
If there isn't enough water in the pipes, sometimes the heater goes out.

23
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:19,070
If this happens you'll need to press this button to reset the heater.

24
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:24,280
Hold it in for about five seconds and the heater should come on again.

25
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:30,240
Then there's a little square indicator under the third knob that's a kind of alarm light.

26
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,800
It'll flash if you need to reset the heater.

27
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,440
It sounds complicated...

28
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:38,500
I'm sure you won't have any problems with it.

29
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,310
There should be some more instructions on the side of the heater.

30
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,700
Call me back if you can't make it work.

31
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,330
Okay.

32
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:52,642
While you're on the phone, we haven't managed to find a few things we need,

33
00:01:52,642 --> 00:01:57,600
like extra pillows for the beds and some washing powder. Is there any here?

34
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:01,200
Pillows... yes. If you look in the cupboard,

35
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:06,580
the large white one upstairs-to the left of the bathroom door

36
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:10,200
There should be four or five on the top shelf.

37
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,480
And if you want to do some washing

38
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:18,460
there's some powder for that... probably by the back door.

39
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,380
There's a kind of shelf there above the sink.

40
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:25,240
In fact, I'm sure there's some there, in a large blue box

41
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:28,500
You need about half a cup full for each wash.

42
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:36,500
And that reminds me, the spare key to the back door is hanging on a hook on the wall by the sitting room window.

43
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,850
Please make sure to put it back when you've used it.

44
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:43,880
The previous guests lost it in the garden and I had to get another one made!

45
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:46,820
And if you have any trouble with the lamps

46
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:50,190
you'll find some spare bulbs in a large cardboard box.

47
00:02:50,190 --> 00:02:54,540
It's on top of the washing machine with all kinds of useful things in it.

48
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:58,710
Oh, and another thing I forgot to mention when we last spoke...

49
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,460
Yes?

50
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:03,930
I've left you a local map, so you'll be able to find your way around easily.

51
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:06,060
It shows the whole area

52
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:10,610
I put it in the top drawer of the chest under the TV in your bedroom.

53
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:13,850
There's a whole file of local information in there too.

54
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:18,690
Thanks. What about visiting the town? Can you give us any advice?

55
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:22,090
Yes. You'll need to take the car.

56
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,660
It's too far to walk from the flat, really.

57
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:28,700
You have to pay to leave your car in all the car parks now I'm afraid

58
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,252
I like the one that's by the station best

59
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:34,680
and you can walk to the town centre from there in five minutes.

60
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:37,000
That's where all the best restaurants are.

61
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,210
But if you want a takeaway, the Italian one does really good pasta and pizzas.

62
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:51,460
Call 7-3 double 2,8-1for that one, or 7 double 6, double 1, 9 for the Chinese.

63
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:54,890
They're both good and they'll both deliver to the flat.

64
00:03:54,890 --> 00:04:01,180
As for places to visit, yes, do go and see the railway museum.

65
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,220
The exhibition is small but really good.

66
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:09,963
It gets very crowded on Sundays, so I suggest you visit it on a quieter day,

67
00:04:09,963 --> 00:04:12,800
later in the week, but not on Thursdays

68
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:16,066
which is market day. You won't find anywhere to park

69
00:04:16,066 --> 00:04:21,450
and it's also the only day of the week when they're not open! Anything else?

70
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,750
Not for the moment. Thanks!
